-    b.  **Compute Product**: Multiply the Gabor Gaussian $G_i(\mathbf{u})$ by the filter Gaussian $F(\mathbf{u})$ in the frequency domain. Since both are Gaussians, their product is another Gaussian $G'_i(\mathbf{u})$ [S1, S2, S3].
